# Missing intermediate certificate for memoria.bn.gov.br (Hemeroteca Digital
# Brasileira / DocReader host).
#
# Problem: memoria.bn.gov.br's TLS handshake serves only its leaf certificate
# (CN=*.bn.gov.br, issued by "Certum DV TLS G2 R39 CA") and omits the
# intermediate that chains it up to a root trusted by strict verifiers
# (OpenSSL, Python's `ssl`/`httpx` via certifi). Confirmed with:
#   echo | openssl s_client -connect memoria.bn.gov.br:443 -showcerts
# — exactly one CERTIFICATE block comes back. Browsers and curl/macOS
# succeed anyway because they either cache this intermediate already or
# fetch it opportunistically via AIA (Authority Information Access)
# chasing; strict clients correctly refuse to complete the chain and fail
# with CERTIFICATE_VERIFY_FAILED / unable to get local issuer certificate.
# This is documented server-side housekeeping, not a sandbox artifact or a
# reason to distrust the endpoint — see docs/access.md §3 (Task 2 finding)
# and docs/docreader-endpoints.md.
#
# How this file was obtained (2026-08-31):
#   1. Extracted the leaf cert's Authority Information Access extension:
#        openssl x509 -in leaf.pem -noout -text | grep -A2 "Authority Information Access"
#      -> CA Issuers - URI:http://certumdvtlsg2r39ca.repository.certum.pl/certumdvtlsg2r39ca.cer
#   2. Downloaded that CA Issuers URL (DER format) and converted to PEM:
#        curl http://certumdvtlsg2r39ca.repository.certum.pl/certumdvtlsg2r39ca.cer -o certum.der
#        openssl x509 -inform DER -in certum.der -out bn-intermediate.pem
#   3. Verified the chain completes against certifi's root bundle:
#        openssl verify -CAfile "$(python3 -c 'import certifi;print(certifi.where())')" \
#          -untrusted bn-intermediate.pem leaf.pem
#      -> leaf.pem: OK
#
# Subject: C=PL, O=Asseco Data Systems S.A., CN=Certum DV TLS G2 R39 CA
# Issuer:  C=PL, O=Asseco Data Systems S.A., OU=Certum Certification Authority,
#          CN=Certum Trusted Root CA
# SHA-256 fingerprint: 83:C0:A5:A7:68:44:C8:40:DF:AF:82:0F:FD:02:AD:F6:
#                      57:3A:26:82:3E:F6:AF:75:8A:33:84:A0:AC:04:40:83
#
# Usage: load alongside certifi's bundle in an ssl.SSLContext, e.g.
#   ctx = ssl.create_default_context(cafile=certifi.where())
#   ctx.load_verify_locations(cafile="src/wrb/certs/bn-intermediate.pem")
# Never use verify=False as a substitute for this.
